<title>POLAND: POLISH NEW CAR SALES UP 30.5 IN JAN-JUNE.</title>
<headline>POLISH NEW CAR SALES UP 30.5 IN JAN-JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car sales in Poland grew by</p>
<p>30.45 percent in January-June against the same period last year</p>
<p>to 262,219 units, an independent car market monitoring agency,</p>
<p>Samar, said in a report.</p>
<p>Samar said sales of commercial vehicles rose 16.8 percent</p>
<p>to 25,933 over the same period. Fiat topped the list of</p>
<p>passenger makers with 90,522 units sold and a 34.5 percent</p>
<p>market share.</p>
<p>				 PASSENGER CARS</p>
<p>		   SALES (UNITS)	  MARKET SHARE (PCT)</p>
<p>	    Jan-June 97  Jan-June 96  Jan-June 97  Jan-June 96</p>
<p>1.Fiat	90,522	 84,275	  34.5	   41.9</p>
<p>2.Daewoo    65,679	 42,325	  25.1	   21.1</p>
<p>3.GM-Opel   22,848	 14,563	   8.7	    7.2</p>
<p>4.Renault   13,872	 14,418	   5.3	    7.2</p>
<p>5.Skoda     11,453	  7,180	   4.4	    3.6</p>
<p>6.Ford	10,126	  5,940	   3.9	    3.0</p>
<p>7.SEAT	 8,106	  5,410	   3.1	    2.7</p>
<p>8.Volkswagen 7,770	  5,803	   3.0	    2.9</p>
<p>9.Peugeot    6,178	  4,367	   2.4	    2.2</p>
<p>10.Citroen   5,960	  3,123	   2.3	    1.6</p>
<p>				  COMMERCIAL VEHICLES</p>
<p>			SALES (UNITS)	   MARKET SHARE (PCT)</p>
<p>		 Jan-June 97 Jan-June 96   Jan-June 97  Jan-June 96</p>
<p>1.Daewoo-Lublin 6,493	5,376	  25.0	  24.2</p>
<p>2.Daewoo	  6,415	8,159	  24.7	  36.7</p>
<p>3.Fiat	    2,719	3,269	  10.5	  14.7</p>
<p>4.Citroen	 2,447	1,204	   9.4	   5.4</p>
<p>5.Ford	    1,534	  873	   5.9	   3.9</p>
